&lt;!-- format as YYYY, or YYYY-YYYY --&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A series of fountain statues have been found, of which two could belong to the same decorative group as a nearby public nympheum close to one of the city’s fora. The first statue-fountain, in the Archaeological Museum of Cordoba, represents a marble female figure in the form of a nymph with a shell, similar to another found in a private collection, of which only the lower part with the remains of a shell still exists. The similarities between the two indicate their manufacture in a workshop in the city itself, which from the style suggests a date around the second century AD.&lt;/p&gt;
